{{Quote|Brock is a smack-talking video game enthusiast. His big attitude hides a more introverted personality, but he'll still do whatever it takes to win!}}
{{Portrait}}
Brock is a {{Rarity|Rare}} [[Brawler]] who has low health, a long range, and a high damage output, but a moderately slow reload speed. He was one of the 15 Brawlers who released at the first Beta launch. His attack shoots long-ranged rockets that explode and deal area damage in a short radius, leaving a fire puddle. His Super fires a barrage of rockets in a large area, destroying obstacles and dealing massive damage. His first Gadget, Rocket Laces, allows him to fire at his feet, damaging nearby enemies and knock them back, and launching Brock into the air. His second Gadget, Rocket Fuel, makes Brock's next attack a mega rocket that has a larger explosion radius, destroys walls and travels faster. His first Star Power, More Rockets!, increases the number of rockets fired from his Super. His second Star Power, Rocket No. Four, increases Brock's ammo capacity to 4. His Hypercharge, Rocket Barrage, increases the number of rockets fired from his next Super, which deal high damage.

==Attack: Rockin' Rocket==
{{Quote|Brock lets fly with a single Rockin' Rocket that really goes the distance.}} Brock's attack is a long-ranged rocket missile that deals high area damage in a 1.5-tile splash radius on impact. After exploding, it sets the ground on fire within a 1-tile radius for 2.9 seconds, dealing 30% of the rocket's damage per second. Unlike other marksmen with longer attack cooldowns, Brock's attack has a much faster cooldown, however, his attacks reload rather slowly and travel slowly as well. Brock takes 0.4 seconds to complete his attack.

==Super: Rocket Rain==
{{Quote|Brock fires a rocket barrage that takes out enemies and obstacles. He only wants to see you bathing in the Rocket Rain!}}When Brock's Super is used, he launches a volley of 9 rockets at 0.2-second intervals spread out over a large area, dealing heavy damage to any targets hit. These rockets can be fired over obstacles and destroy terrain within a 1.5-tile splash radius, but they can't set the ground on fire. The Super has an extremely long cooldown and takes 2.05 seconds to complete. Brock can still move while Rocket Rain is in effect, and the rockets fired move along with him. However, he can't attack or reload while using his Super, and it is cancelled if Brock is knocked back, pulled, or stunned. 

==Gadgets==
===Rocket Laces===
{{Quote|Brock jumps to a targeted area, knocking back nearby enemies on takeoff and landing and dealing minor damage. Cooldown: 22 seconds.}}
{{Gadget|1}}
When used, Brock jumps up to 4 tiles in the aimed direction, making an explosion on takeoff and landing, and allowing him to jump over walls or water. Any enemy in the explosion is knocked back and takes 1000 damage. The explosion has a radius of 2 tiles, and can't destroy walls or bushes. If required to cross over a larger amount of blocks or over lakes, his jumping distance will be increased up to a limit or to the nearest piece of ground. While in the air, Brock is completely immune to all damage besides status effects and damage applied over time. Auto-aiming this Gadget will aim it in your direction of movement. This Gadget's cooldown begins after the attack is used.

{{Quote|Hitting an enemy Brawler gives +2 sec movement speed.}}{{Buffie|Gadget}}
With the Buffie, after hitting an enemy Brawler with the Gadget, Brock will also receive 30% movement speed boost for 2 seconds. 

===Rocket Fuel===
{{Quote|Brock fires a large rocket that destroys terrain and deals damage. Cooldown: 22 seconds.}}
{{Gadget|2}}
When aiming using the Gadget button, Brock shoots a rocket which destroys obstacles and deals 86.21% the damage as one of his main attack rocket. This attack does not deal extra damage and does not have the fire effect. This Gadget's cooldown begins after the attack is used.

{{Quote|The rocket breaks into 4 smaller rockets after exploding that also do damage.}}{{Buffie|Gadget}}
With the Buffie, after the rocket hits an obstacle or enemy Brawler, the rocket breaks into 4 smaller rockets which deal 25% the damage as the large rocket.

==Star Powers==
===More Rockets!===
{{Quote|Rocket Rain now rains down 44% more rockets.}}{{StarPower|1}}Brock's Super now fires 4 more rockets, increasing the number of rockets from 9 to 13. This Star Power also decreases the time between rockets by 25%, but slightly increases the total Super time by 0.2 seconds.

{{Quote|Brock gains 20% movement speed while firing his Super.}}{{Buffie|Star}}
With the Buffie, Brock's movement speed is increased by 20% while using his Super.

===Rocket No. 4===
{{Quote|Brock loads a fourth rocket into his launcher, increasing his ammo capacity (and discarding the thermos bottle he's been keeping in his launcher's #4 tube).}}{{StarPower|2}}Brock gains an extra ammo bar, allowing him to have up to 4 attacks ready at once, instead of 3. However, Brock's reload speed remains the same, so it takes 33% longer for him to fully reload all his ammo after firing all four rockets.

{{Quote|Every 8 sec Brock's next attack has increased range.}}{{Buffie|Star}}
With the Buffie, Brock gains a charge bar which takes 8 seconds to charge, and when charged, Brock's next rocket range gets increased by 2 tiles. A radar symbol will glow above Brock's head, along with a sound effect, signaling the charged attack. The aiming reticle will also turn green.

==Hypercharge: Rocket Barrage==
{{Quote|Rockets fired during the Super are cluster bombs.}}{{Hypercharge}}
When activated, Brock's next Super fires 4 waves of 7 rockets, each rocket dealing 800 damage, or 840 damage if he has the Hypercharge damage boost. If Brock has his More Rockets Star Power equipped, his Super will fire 5 waves of 7 rockets instead. He also gains a 20% speed boost, a 5% damage boost, and a 5% shield boost.

{{Quote|Rockin' Rockets fires an additional two small rockets, each dealing 40% damage of the main rocket.}}{{Buffie|Hyper}}
With the Buffie, during his Hypercharge, Brock fires two additional small rockets which move parallelly and deal 40% damage that of the normal rocket. Increased Hypercharge duration by 2 seconds.

